// Keep the NVIDIA driver out of unattended-upgrades on Pea.
//
// The driver ships as a userspace library, which switches over the moment the
// package installs, and a kernel module, which switches only on reboot. With
// Automatic-Reboot off, an unattended driver upgrade leaves the host
// half-upgraded: running containers keep serving, but nvidia-smi fails with
// "Driver/library version mismatch" and no GPU container can start or be
// recovered until someone reboots (2026-10-10, 580.173.02 -> 580.178.04).
//
// Every other security update stays automatic. Upgrade the driver on purpose:
// docs/nvidia-driver-upgrades.md. Installed by install-driver-upgrade-guard.sh.
// Entries are regular expressions matched against package names.
Unattended-Upgrade::Package-Blacklist {
    "nvidia-";
    "libnvidia-";
    "xserver-xorg-video-nvidia-";
};
